{{!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     home/follow — the handles.
     ------------------------------------------------------------------------
     Renders only when at least one handle is set: an empty row of icons is
     worse than no band. {{#social_accounts}} yields nothing when Admin →
     Settings → Social accounts is empty, but footer/social always appends RSS,
     so the emptiness test has to be the handles themselves.
     ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ --}}
{{#social_accounts @site}}
    {{#if @first}}
        <section class="ns-band ns-band--tight">
            <div class="ns-band__inner">
                <div class="ns-band__head ns-band__head--center">
                    <span class="ns-kicker">{{t "Elsewhere"}}</span>
                    <h2 class="ns-band__title">{{t "Follow along while it is built"}}</h2>
                    <p class="ns-band__lede">{{t "Work in progress gets posted as it happens — drafts, teardowns, and the parts that did not work."}}</p>
                </div>
                {{!-- The row's `display: flex` comes from `.ns-footer__col ul`
                     in NSDS, not from `.ns-footer__social` itself — that class
                     only sets flex-DIRECTION. Outside a footer column there is
                     no flex context to give a direction to, so the icons stack
                     vertically. Three utilities supply the context here rather
                     than wrapping a band in a footer class it is not part of. --}}
                {{> "footer/social" class="ns-footer__social flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-2"}}
            </div>
        </section>
    {{/if}}
{{/social_accounts}}
